            "body": "Validated on our 8×H20-3e (TP=8 + EP) setup with DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731 + DSpark\nspeculative decoding — **the fix works.**\n\n- Built from PR head `69a7fb3` (Python layer from this branch; precompiled CUDA\n  kernels from a newer nightly wheel artifact — see note below)\n- `pytest tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_mega_moe.py::test_dspark_skips_unregistered_expert_weight` — **passed**\n- Startup no longer raises `KeyError: routed_experts.w13_weight_scale` — unmapped\n  draft weights are skipped silently and real weights load normally: all 48\n  checkpoint shards loaded in 12.2s (v0.26 skip semantics restored)\n- Serve-level: blocked by an op-signature mismatch between the precompiled nightly\n  artifact and the PR-head Python layer (`_C::gptq_marlin_repack() expected at\n  most 5 argument(s) but received 6`) during `process_weights_after_loading` —\n  an artifact of my mixed source/wheel build, separate from this PR's scope\n  (weight loading), which is confirmed fixed.\n\nNote: I dropped the `--kv-offloading-*` flags from my original repro command\n(separate upstream issue, unrelated to this loader fix).\n\nThanks @cr-zhao for the fix!\n",
